course: dictionary
lesson: 5681
title: The lobe: a round part that sticks out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lobe is a round part that sticks out from something. Your earlobe is the soft, round bit at the bottom of your ear. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. Here, «round» and «sticks out» tell you what a lobe looks like.
explain: Scientists use lobe for a round part of an organ, such as a lung or the brain. «The right lung has three lobes, the left two.» The word lobes is the same word, used in a science lesson. The clue is that each lobe is one part of a bigger organ.
explain: Leaves can have lobes too. «Oak leaves have rounded lobes» means the leaf has round parts that stick out from its edge. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Oak leaves have rounded parts that stick out» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «A coot has flat flaps called lobes» on its toes, and these flaps spread when it swims. A lobe can be an earlobe, part of a brain, or part of a leaf, but each time it is a rounded part.
fact: A lobe is a rounded part that sticks out.
fact: Your earlobe is the soft, round part at the bottom of your ear.
fact: The brain has lobes, such as the frontal, parietal, temporal and occipital lobes, and each does a different job.
fact: «The ginkgo's name biloba means two lobes, after the split leaf.»
fact: A coot's toe lobes spread when it swims and fold when it walks.
exercise: «The ginkgo's name biloba means two lobes, after the split leaf.» What is a lobe here? | A bird's beak | *A rounded part that sticks out | A flat sheet of paper | A kind of tree
exercise: Where is your earlobe? | *The soft, round part at the bottom of your ear | The top of your head | Inside your nose | The tip of your finger
exercise: «A coot has flat flaps called lobes that spread when swimming and fold when walking.» What do the lobes do when the coot swims? | *They spread out | They disappear | They turn into feathers | They fold up
test: How many lobes does the right lung have? | Five | Two | *Three | One
test: Which of these is a lobe of the brain? | Earlobe | Toe flap | Leaf stalk | *Frontal lobe
exam: In «Oak leaves have rounded lobes», what does lobes mean? | A sharp, spiky tip | A flat green colour | A tiny insect | *Rounded parts that stick out
